## Model card

- **Name:** GPT-5 nano
- **Short description:** OpenAI’s GPT-5 nano is an ultra-compact, low-cost reasoning model tier (400K context, 128K max output) for high-volume classification/extraction and lightweight tasks; deprecated/superseded by newer nano tiers.
- **Provider / access:** OpenAI API (`gpt-5-nano`, snapshot `gpt-5-nano-2025-08-07`, deprecated). Local metadata lists `opencode/gpt-5-nano`, pricing $0.05/$0.40 per 1M, and `noFreeId`.
- **Release / knowledge:** OpenAI model docs reviewed 2026-11-10. Knowledge cutoff listed as 2024-05-31 in docs.
- **IDs:** `gpt-5-nano`, `gpt-5-nano-2025-08-07`.
- **Context window:** 400,000 tokens total (272,000 max input noted in docs); 128,000 max output.
- **Modalities:** Text and image input; text output.
- **Pricing (as of 2026-11-10):** $0.05/$0.40 per 1M in/out, $0.005 cached input (OpenAI docs).
- **Architecture:** Proprietary closed model. Architecture/parameter count not publicly disclosed.

